Move the two attributes the convention has no key for under one vendor-scoped
prefix. `genai.usage.is_partial` is now `claude_agent_sdk.usage.is_partial` and
`gen_ai.usage.cost_usd` is now `claude_agent_sdk.usage.cost_usd`. This is a
visible output change: a dashboard or query reading either of the old names will
stop finding it. Neither collided with a real semconv key, but they disagreed with
each other, a custom key under `gen_ai.*` squats on a name a future semconv cost
attribute will claim, and `genai.` is one character from the real namespace and
reads as a typo.
